$meta
  title = Red Storm Rising
  description = Cold War tactical submarine warfare in the North Atlantic, 1988. Command USS Dallas against the Soviet Northern Fleet — passive sonar, target motion analysis, wire-guided torpedoes, and the campaign for the GIUK gap.
  tags = submarine, simulation, wargame, cold war, navy, atlantic, sonar, tactical
  header
    mode = minimal

radioChatter
  (unintelligible Russian HF traffic)
  — K-414 to Group: sonar contact, bearing two-one-zero. Possible submarine.
  — Comrade Admiral, permission to increase speed to 22 knots.
  (distant sonar transducer ping)
  — Watch your datum, the screen is thin tonight.
  (faint music and laughter from a long-range broadcast)
  — Missile boat reports all tubes ready, sailing in twelve hours.
  (static crackle, then silence)

damageReports
  HIT! WE ARE UNDER ATTACK
  FLOODING IN THE TORPEDO ROOM!
  FIRE IN AUXILIARY MACHINERY!
  WE ARE UNDER ATTACK — ALARM!
  HULL PRESSURE WAVE — DAMAGE CONTROL PARTIES AWAY

newsSnippets
  NATO CINCLANT: convoy HX-214 delivered safe to Liverpool.
  TASS reports 40,000 tons of NATO shipping sunk in the Atlantic.
  Soviet Backfires hit a resupply convoy; two escorts lost.
  Keflavik reports heavy ASW activity in the GIUK gap.
  Naval intelligence: Kirov refueled at sea, proceeding west.
  Two Soviet SSBNs tracked leaving Kola for patrol stations.
